---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<Base
  title="About Muhammad Farooqui — E-Commerce Operator, Karachi"
  description="Muhammad Farooqui is an e-commerce operator and D2C brand builder from Karachi who runs the whole business: storefront, ads, courier operations and margins."
  ogType="profile"
>
  <header class="pagehead">
    <p class="eyebrow">About / Muhammad Farooqui</p>
    <h1>Close to the work.<br /><em>Accountable to the whole.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">I build e-commerce brands and work across the systems that keep them running. My base is Karachi. My focus is the full business.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="essay">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div><strong>Based in</strong>Karachi, Pakistan</div>
      <div><strong>Owned projects</strong>AEEN · MOG</div>
      <div><strong>Focus</strong>Shopify · Growth · Operations</div>
      <div><strong>Company</strong><a href={site.company.url}>{site.company.name}</a></div>
    </aside>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The storefront is only the start.</h2>
      <p>A customer sees a product, an ad and a checkout. Behind that simple journey are decisions about the catalogue, creative, fulfilment, courier payments and margins. I work across those decisions.</p>
      <p>AEEN (<a href={site.aeen.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{site.aeen.domain}</a>) is my eyewear brand. MOG, Mart of Gadget, is my gadget store. They are the context for my work with Shopify, custom product experiences and day-to-day e-commerce operations. Across platforms, I have managed more than PKR 14 crore in ad spend.</p>
      <h2>How I approach the work</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Understand the whole order.</strong> Trace the path from acquisition to cash received before changing one part in isolation.</li>
        <li><strong>Find the actual constraint.</strong> Separate a weak offer from a slow page, a delivery issue or a cost problem.</li>
        <li><strong>Build something inspectable.</strong> A working page, an order workflow or a clear reconciliation sheet beats a vague recommendation.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep the feedback loop open.</strong> Review what happened, document limitations and decide what to improve next.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Practical systems, human judgement.</h2>
      <p>I use custom Shopify code and AI-assisted workflows where they make the work better. Tools support the business; they do not replace an understanding of the product, the customer or the numbers. I am the person you deal with, with a team behind me for execution.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <CTA />
</Base>
